# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PorcoBench .gitignore
#
# Rule: code, docs, manifests and run *records* (hashes, timings, verdicts)
# are versioned. Benchmark instances and anything that reproduces their
# content or their solutions stay local: CNFs, proofs, witnesses/models and
# solver stdout. Not every instance is cleared for redistribution (see
# manifest.csv license_status), and the proofs alone are >100 GB. Recreate
# them with scripts/fetch_corpus.py, scripts/build_tools.sh and the harnesses.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python / OS / editors ---------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv*/
venv/
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Local toolchain builds and download caches ------------------------------
# Kissat and drat-trim are rebuilt at pinned commits by scripts/build_tools.sh
.tools/
# GBD metadata and fetch logs written by build_benchmark.py
.cache/

# --- Benchmark instances (fetched + hash-verified by scripts/fetch_corpus.py) -
cnf/
*.cnf
*.cnf.xz
*.dimacs

# --- Instance-derived evidence: proofs, witnesses, models, solver output -----
*.drat
*.drat.gz
proof.*
witness.txt
witness.json
solve.stdout
# FPGA per-attempt records embed the solver model (raw_stack / model); the
# per-attempt outcome, cycles and timings are published in results.csv
calibration/pigweed-fpga-*/attempts/
# private decompressed inputs and the frozen third-party candidate copy
# (PigWeedSAT, Apache-2.0; pinned by commit in run.json)
calibration/*/inputs/
calibration/*/candidate/

# --- Superseded or archival local-only runs ----------------------------------
# aborted cpu-v0 attempts (pre-fix harness; zero terminal records)
calibration/cpu-v0-aborted-attempt*
# rejected first-attach run, kept locally as incident evidence
calibration/stale/

# --- Never commit credentials ------------------------------------------------
credentials.json
*.key
.env

# run-directory flock files (empty, process-local)
.lock
